      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Let me also check if `ExecutionVisitor` is defined somewhere in the project.Let me check the working directory and compile script setup.Now I have a clear picture. The original test references `ExecutionVisitor` which is a private inner class in `SequencesComparatorTest` — it can't compile as a standalone file. I'll write an improved version that:\n1. Includes the `ExecutionVisitor` inner class (required for compilation)\n2. Renames `sequence()` → `toCharList()` for clarity\n3. Extracts named local variables in the loop to avoid calling `toCharList()` twice with the same argument\n4. Adds a meaningful assertion message identifying which pair failed\n5. Adds a Javadoc comment on the test method\n6. Removes unused imports (`assertTrue`, `Random`)"
